WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.270
<i>Just three kilometers left.</i>

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.650
<i>I'll take the finish line alone.</i>

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.430
Kyoto Fushimi's in the lead!

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.900
Wow, seriously?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.160
Kyoto Fushimi's #111, Midousuji, 
is the first to come up the hill!

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.170
<i>At least, I was supposed to.</i>

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.910
And behind him is...

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.650
<i>But you're the only one who 
didn't take his eyes off me...</i>

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.630
<i>You chicken-headed bean!</i>

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.140
You should be thanking me, Midousuji.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.880
I thought you'd be bored traveling 
alone, so I tagged along.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.450
Sohoku's in second! It's Naruko!

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.640
He's keeping up with Midousuji by himself!

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.970
<i>He shifted up.</i>

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.020
<i>This guy...</i>

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.240
<i>He's stronger than he was last winter!</i>

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.480
<i>That massive pressure was real!</i>

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.560
Oh, right.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.790
Chicken-head, as a special treat, 
I'll show you something special.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.210
I still have something special up my sleeve.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.630
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.720
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:45.620
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:47.370
<i>LINE.04 Five Men's Resolve</i>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.020
Things are buzzing over here.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.640
Sawada-kun and Gorizo-kun 
saved us spots to watch the finish.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:55.630
Sohoku High School

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.360
We did it!

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.690
At high speed!

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.610
Bro, when will you get here?

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.850
Oh, how was the race?

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.990
We took the school bus.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.490
Listen, Sadatoki.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.530
Sounds like the leaders will be here soon.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.820
We'll be waiting!

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.070
Keep up the pace, please!

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.410
This is third-year Koga.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.320
Sadatoki, listen closely.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.590
The support car is stuck in 
a traffic jam at Irohazaka.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.800
After taking the spare bikes to the 
feed zone and handing off supplies,

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.900
we were fortunate enough to 
be picked up by the news car.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:27.390
<b>News Car</b>

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:27.390
We're on our way there now, 
but I don't know if we'll make it in time.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:31.440
You first-years who are there will 
have to support Sohoku alone.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.200
What?

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.720
Koga-san, are you serious?

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.260
But we're first-years!

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.820
This is our first Inter-High!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.000
Sawada and Gorizo,
 you and the other first-years

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.790
will prepare to receive our 
riders after the finish line.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.650
Give them ice water, towels,
 and water bottles.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.030
<i>Y-Yes, sir!</i>

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.490
<i>High speed!</i>

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.080
Sadatoki, you'll cheer for them.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.430
Huh? Cheer?

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.660
<i>Our riders are giving everything they have.</i>

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:01.090
<i>At the very, very end, they draw strength 
from their teammates' support.</i>

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.640
<i>Help them win with your voice!</i>

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.390
<i>With your cheers!</i>

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.470
B-But, I...

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.900
No buts! Do it!

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:10.980
You're the only one who can!

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.270
<i>It's an important job.</i>

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.640
<i>Push them with your voice.</i>

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.830
<i>Make sure your voice isn't 
drowned out by the others.</i>

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.530
<i>It's okay, Sadatoki.</i>

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.190
You can do it. I know you can.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.680
Your brother knows you can.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.530
It's okay. Your voice is 
louder than the others.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.690
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.370
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.300
<i>I can...</i>

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.550
<i>For everyone...</i>

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:45.740
Understood!

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.780
Sohoku, fight!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.250
Tadokoro Bread

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.830
We made it! The leaders aren't here yet!

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.240
What did you think of my driving?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:09.740
Looks like we'll get to see 
the finish, Makishima, Kinjou.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.550
I-It sucks.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:16.610
My flight was six hours late, 
and then that crazy car ride...

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:21.240
Y-You took a road that wasn't on the map.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.590
I'm impressed, Tadokoro.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.510
Don't feel like you have to compliment him.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.430
So, this where it is this year.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.680
Yeah. Nikkou City, Tochigi Prefecture.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.430
On the northwest side of Lake Chuzenji

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.560
is Senjougahara, a marsh stretching across
 the terrain at 1,400 meters above sea level.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.520
The eruptions of Mount Nantaisan formed a lake

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:45.190
that became a marsh over 
a long period of time.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:49.570
National Route 120 cuts through Senjougahara.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:53.640
And the Sanbonmatsu Park 
parking lot gate is

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.580
the finish line of day one of 
the Tochigi Inter-High.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.140
I haven't felt this tension 
and anticipation in a while.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.300
Yeah. I can't get enough of this atmosphere.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.230
Just thinking about it 
sends chills down my spine.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:12.140
You can really feel that unique 
sensation of the Inter-High.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.090
You're right.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:21.860
So, who's going to be first?

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.900
Imaizumi, as the ace?

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.210
You might be surprised.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.950
It could be that little red bean.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.010
They're entering the flat 
before the finish line!

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:38.040
Kyoto Fushimi removed some kind of tape!

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:40.920
<i>Midousuji's playing the ace up his sleeve!</i>

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.980
<i>Unleashing both legs.</i>

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:48.550
<i>This is the trump card
 I've been saving until now.</i>

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:57.930
You still haven't fallen, 
chicken-headed bean!

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.100
The road's wide enough!

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.430
Stay away from me, Gross-suji!

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.390
I'm on fire now, Midousuji!

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:04.770
My blood is boiling!

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:09.950
Then maybe you should go to 
the hospital, chicken-head!

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:13.950
I'll go to any hospital,
as long as it's red and flashy!

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.470
<i>Chicken-head...</i>

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.780
<i>This little bean has gotten stronger.</i>

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:24.850
<i>He improved his climbing, but he 
hasn't gotten slower on the flats.</i>

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:28.760
<i>If anything, it feels like he's applying 
his climbing muscles to the flats.</i>

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.710
<i>Not bad.</i>

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:36.600
<i>Come to think of it, Ishigaki-kun 
mentioned something last winter.</i>

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:42.900
Naruko-kun might return to racing.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.650
Huh? What makes you say that?

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:53.030
Midousuji, disappointment 
makes people stronger.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.910
<i>Bring it on.</i>

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.500
<i>I'll overthrow your strength and 
wrest the victory from your hands.</i>

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.000
One kilometer left!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.370
<i>I'm getting chills.
 My hair's standing on end.</i>

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:08.630
<i>I'm in a make-or-break race with Midousuji</i>

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.550
<i>on the flat before the 
Inter-High's finish line.</i>

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.430
<i>A thousand meters remain!</i>

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.760
<i>Tons of fans are watching!</i>

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.060
<i>If this isn't flashy...</i>

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.560
<i>I don't know what is!</i>

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.310
There are 900 meters left!

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.230
Kyoto Fushimi is pulling ahead!

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.490
Good, Midousuji. This is the best.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:31.110
I'm burning up. Let's do this.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.990
Let's put our lives on the line!

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:40.240
He's so fast! Sohoku's keeping up!

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.750
They're seriously amazing!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.220
I can feel their spirit from over here!

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:48.340
So it's come down to those two.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.640
The next three have made it up the hill!

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:02.430
<i>How far behind are we?</i>

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.190
<i>Three-hundred and fifty meters.</i>

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.770
<i>We're so far behind.</i>

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:11.160
<i>It'll be hard to catch up from here.</i>

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.850
<i>But Naruko's with him.</i>

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:16.950
<i>This isn't a bad development for Sohoku!</i>

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.680
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.210
<i>All the pride Hakone Academy has built up...</i>

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:24.410
<i>Was our riding not good enough?</i>

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.320
<i>I got our ace this far.</i>

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.600
<i>Me, the Black Cat Deliveryman.</i>

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:33.630
<i>And because of just one stupid 
mistake, the finish line...</i>

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.490
If you've got time to think, ride, Yukinori!

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:39.970
Let's go, Takuto!

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.270
It's okay, Yuki-chan.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.330
Huh?

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.520
The two of us can't close this gap.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.340
Even if the two of you pull,
 we'll never catch up.

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:56.970
But with the three of us,
 we may be able to reach them.

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:04.100
There's no point if the ace doesn't 
save his strength for the finish line.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:10.500
But unless you're in front of the finish line,
 there's nothing to race for.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.950
I'll pull.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:19.160
We... Hakone Academy has 
nothing left to lose!

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:27.890
Hakone Academy's ace Ashikiba-san 
is making his move!

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:34.480
<i>Their ace moved to the front.</i>

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:39.660
<i>He's helping us catch up 
to Midousuji and Naruko.</i>

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.700
<i>He's fast. He's huge.</i>

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:46.240
<i>He towers over me,
 and I'm 180 centimeters tall.</i>

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:50.420
<i>Standing at 202 centimeters,
 he's the tallest man at the race.</i>

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.670
<i>His wind pressure is incredible.</i>

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:56.300
Takuto, is there classical 
music playing inside your head?

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.380
Yes.

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:03.080
<i>The clichéd Ninth!</i>

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.920
<i>The Ninth Symphony!</i>

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:12.900
Keep it up, Takuto!

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.750
They're catching up!

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.270
Hakone Academy's ace is pulling!

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:20.360
Only Sohoku and Kyoto Fushimi 
have riders in the lead group!

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.930
Will they catch up?

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.030
Their rotation has increased their speed...

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.700
But there's only one kilometer left!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.440
<i>We'll catch up. We'll catch up.</i>

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.000
<i>We're slowly closing the gap.</i>

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:37.380
<i>Yuki-chan carried me this 
far so I could rest.</i>

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.480
<i>The classical music is playing.</i>

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:41.010
<i>My heart is pounding.</i>

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:47.880
<i>I never thought I'd get to be in the Inter-High,
 but here I am turning my pedals.</i>

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:51.480
<i>On top of that, I'm wearing 
Hakone Academy's #1 tag.</i>

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:55.810
<i>Me, the team's best laundry boy!</i>

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.810
<b>Club Chores</b>

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.280
What do you want to be?

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.750
The best ri...

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:09.490
...rider.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.490
What do you like?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.710
The piano.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:15.630
Good.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.210
Use that to ride.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.680
Let it push you forward.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.650
<i>I finally achieved something.</i>

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:24.840
<i>But...</i>

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.170
<i>No way. No way.</i>

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.400
<i>Why can't I win?</i>

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.430
<i>I'm wearing a jersey.</i>

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:36.980
<i>I promised Fukutomi-san I would win.</i>

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:45.070
<i>In that moment, unable to understand 
the situation, my brain got a flat tire.</i>

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:48.520
<i>I tried to reset everything.</i>

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:52.610
<i>I was racing to repay their kindness.</i>

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.870
<i>But I couldn't think anymore.</i>

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:01.300
He's riding backward! Watch out!

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.590
<i>I betrayed their expectations.</i>

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.960
I'm placing you on house arrest indefinitely.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:09.810
I'm not letting you race.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.420
You won't race at the Inter-High, either.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.390
I'm sorry.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:18.060
<i>It was a dizzying three years.</i>

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:21.250
<i>A less than laudable three years.</i>

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.850
<i>"Riding backward on the course."</i>

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:26.170
<i>"Indefinitely suspended from racing."</i>

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.290
<i>I screwed up.</i>

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.730
<i>But my teammates supported me.</i>

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:34.420
<i>My seniors forgave me.</i>

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:43.630
Ashikiba, the race for the finish is 
both a physical and mental battle.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:48.590
Tell yourself over and over
 that you are the ace.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.390
That you are strong.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.810
<i>I am strong!</i>

00:13:55.590 --> 00:14:00.110
<i>So these limbs, this body, this number tag...</i>

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:04.440
<i>This opportunity doesn't belong to me!</i>

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.780
<i>Go, Takuto.</i>

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:12.280
<i>You carried such anguish and pain, 
such hopes to make it this far.</i>

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:17.540
<i>I'm racing to repay all the people</i>

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:22.540
<i>who called me the ace!</i>

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:27.760
It's the Hakone Academy ace 
Ashikiba's Metronome Dancing!

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:32.280
The way he swings his giant body 
back and forth is like a metronome!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.330
He's huge!

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.060
He's fast!

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:39.020
<i>I am strong!</i>

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.410
I'm catching up!

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:43.610
I'm catching up to the guys in front!

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.740
Switch with me, Takuto!

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.100
Hakone Academy's Kuroda moved to the front!

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:52.120
Go, Kuroda!

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.910
I'll show you how I pull!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.790
This is Hakone Academy's final effort!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:15:00.390
Bend, Cat Legs!

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:03.860
<i>We'll catch up!</i>

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:07.010
<i>Kyoto's Midousuji and Sohoku's Naruko!</i>

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.470
<i>Take it, Naruko!</i>

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.520
<i>I have to...</i>

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.330
<i>...catch up!</i>

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.410
<i>It's almost...</i>

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:16.010
<i>...the finish line!</i>

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:19.020
The trailing three are chasing after them!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.560
They have the two in front in their sights!

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.980
Is it a five-man finish line sprint?

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:26.620
There are three behind and two in front!

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.040
They have the numbers advantage!

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:33.410
Maybe if there were a thousand 
meters left, but the finish line...

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:36.840
...is 500 meters ahead!

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.660
They're at a disadvantage!

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.890
<i>The running finish.</i>

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:45.030
<i>You're wasting your time, Hakone Academy.</i>

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:51.280
<i>Even if you pool your efforts 
and work your muscles,</i>

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:56.810
<i>this margin at 500 meters remaining...</i>

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:01.100
<i>...was always part of my calculations!</i>

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:08.360
<i>This chicken-head was the only 
thing I didn't account for.</i>

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.690
Why are you staring at me 
like that, Midousuji?

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.330
We're at the finish line.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:16.210
Determination, full power, flashiness...

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.830
Even men fall for my flashiness!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.540
Have you fallen for me, too, Midousuji?

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:27.170
I was just exercising my eyes,
 since they were stinging from all your red,

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.460
chicken-head!

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.960
Gross!

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:35.970
You're determined to interfere 
with my victory, aren't you?

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.560
I'm not just interfering! I'm going to win!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.240
You're in the way! Move!

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:42.270
You're in the way, idiot!

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:45.340
They're crashing into each 
other before the finish line?

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:46.980
Wow!

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:50.250
You're strong.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:54.860
You really are amazing.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:17:00.540
Every time I race against you, 
I have the same thought.

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:08.000
If you had stayed in Kansai for high school 
and joined Kyoto Fushimi with me...

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:16.010
If we'd been on the same team—and maybe 
it's weird for me to say this now...

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:24.350
But I always think of how we could've 
been the best of friends, Naruko-kun.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.740
Don't you agree?

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:31.400
The two of us...

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:35.360
You finished telling lies, Midousuji?

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:39.940
Is this bluff an attempt to distract me
 with warm fuzzy feelings

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:43.620
and kill your opponent's tension 
before the finish line?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.630
You'll do anything to win.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.500
You really are something, Midousuji.

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:50.530
But you won't fool me!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:54.010
You don't think we'd be best friends!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.320
You're right! Not in the slightest!

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:02.310
I've never even considered it!

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.850
<i>So that's what you meant, Naruko.</i>

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:12.070
<i>The day you returned from Osaka, 
you said you raced someone.</i>

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:15.460
Wow, takoyaki.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.460
Who did you race against?

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:16.640
Nobody, really.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.530
It wasn't someone you know.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:22.330
Thanks for the food.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:22.330
<i>But your opponent was...</i>

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:26.040
<i>Midousuji!</i>

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.250
<i>That's why you kept your eyes on him</i>

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:32.810
<i>during the confusion earlier 
and raced after him.</i>

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:37.510
<i>And now you're side by side, 
racing for the finish line.</i>

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:42.800
<i>You should've told me if it 
was that important, Naruko.</i>

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:47.430
I'm the one who told you 
to become an all-rounder!

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:49.420
I made the decision!

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:51.650
Let's race, hotshot.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:52.580
What?

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:55.160
We'll pull ahead of Hakone Academy
 before the finish line.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:55.860
I see.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:59.030
Whoever crosses the finish 
line first is the ace!

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:00.820
Bring it on!

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:03.620
<i>So that's how it is.</i>

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.910
<i>Go, Naruko.</i>

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:10.290
<i>If I catch up to you just 
before the finish line...</i>

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:16.360
<i>I'll push your back as hard as I can!</i>

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.530
<i>Today, you're the ace, Naruko!</i>

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.300
<i>Take the finish line!</i>

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:25.970
The leaders have crossed the 400 meter line!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.630
Sohoku's Naruko is in front!

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:31.940
<i>He refuses to let me have it.</i>

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.450
Then I don't have a choice.

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:40.740
I'll have to fly before the finish line!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:42.610
Fly?

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:47.620
Is Midousuji breaking out 
his true trump card?

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:50.750
The others have crossed the 400-meter line!

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.750
Go, Hakone Academy!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:57.970
<i>We're chasing as fast as we can,
but they're going at top speed, too.</i>

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.260
<i>It's not that easy to close this gap.</i>

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.880
But! But!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.220
It's not easy, but...

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:08.390
There's nothing I can't do!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:17.990
Just 300 meters remaining!

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.690
They're closing the gap!

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.280
Will they stay ahead? Will they catch up?

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.910
<i>I already said they can't catch up.</i>

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:31.000
<i>Actually, if the course were straight, 
they might have.</i>

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:40.490
<i>But there's a difficult corner leading 
the course from National Route 120</i>

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:47.300
<i>to the first day's finish line 
at the large parking lot.</i>

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.760
<i>Two of them.</i>

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.190
<i>I'm entering the corner first!</i>

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.560
<i>I can see it.</i>

00:20:58.010 --> 00:20:59.750
<i>It's the finish line gate!</i>

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:04.210
Time to fly.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.420
When insects have oversaturated an area...

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:20.040
They metamorphosize wings,
so they can fly to new locations!

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:25.950
<i>We're in the middle of a corner, Midousuji!</i>

00:21:25.950 --> 00:21:28.340
<i>You're going to do that here?</i>

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.490
<i>This... is my...</i>

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:38.100
<i>Metamorphosis!</i>

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:15.860
Makishima's late.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:17.560
Yeah.

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:21.430
It's hot.

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:23.220
Yeah.

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:27.340
<b>Six Hours Later</b>

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:32.980
Kinjou, have you gotten tanner?

00:23:32.980 --> 00:23:34.470
You think so?

00:23:36.530 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>NEXT RIDE  3 Seconds Less</i>

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:44.980
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:51.500
<b>Mura</b>
